    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Connect your source\n\nPoint your form, contact page or chat at this webhook (**POST**, JSON body).\n\nExpected fields:\n- name\n- email\n- message\n\n*Tip:* **Listen for test event** and send a test POST.",
        "height": 333,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        1000
      ],
      "id": "b1b1b1b1-1111-4111-8111-bbbbbbbbbbbb",
      "name": "Setup 1"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Connect Claude\n\n1. Open **Claude model**, Credential, *Create new*, and paste your **Anthropic API key**.\n2. Default model: **Haiku 4.5**. Picking one of three labels does not need a large model. Keep the larger ones for writing text.\n\nThe output schema uses `enum`, so a label outside the list fails validation instead of reaching the Switch.",
        "height": 333,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        310,
        1000
      ],
      "id": "b2b2b2b2-2222-4222-8222-bbbbbbbbbbbb",
      "name": "Setup 2"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Connect each branch\n\nEach output ends in a **No Operation** placeholder. Replace it with your action:\n- **Sales**: your CRM, or an alert to a salesperson\n- **Support**: open a ticket or reply\n- **Other**: manual review\n\nClaude returns `category`, `urgency` and `summary`; every branch can use them. Anything that matches no rule goes to **Other**.",
        "height": 354,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        660,
        1000
      ],
      "id": "b3b3b3b3-3333-4333-8333-bbbbbbbbbbbb",
      "name": "Setup 3"
    }
  ],
